At n=40 (the token count of one turn in validate.py) and d=8, n/d=5: the
estimated spectrum is still noise-dominated and rank_eff is nearly
uncorrelated with the truth. Pooling across turns, or tracking the spectrum
on a trailing window of several hundred tokens, is not optional -- it is the
difference between a measurement and a random number.

Bias direction matters for a halt rule: at small n, rank_eff is biased LOW
(noise floor eats real channels), so a dark-mode halt trigger would fire on
healthy sessions -- false positives, not false negatives.
